# Ask Permission Before Usage Actions

Before any action that can consume usage, quota, credits, billing, or paid API calls, ask the user for explicit approval first.

## Usage-consuming actions (approval required)
- Web search or URL fetch tools.
- External API calls or remote MCP tools that can consume quota.
- Browser automation sessions that may consume metered usage.
- Any paid model/tool invocation beyond local file and local shell work.

## No-usage local work (no extra approval needed)
- Reading/editing local files in the workspace.
- Local searches (`rg`, glob) and local lint/build/test runs.
- Local git inspection commands.

## Approval format
- Ask a clear yes/no question before usage actions.
- Name the exact tool/action and why it is needed.
- If denied, continue with no-usage local alternatives.

## Completion behavior
- Do not run usage actions on assumptions.
- If usage is required to unblock, stop and wait for user approval.
